The SingleDatabaseManager class is internal, so I cannot directly instantiate or subclass it in the test project. Since the refactoring tools are not available to make it public or add seams, I will write a test that exercises the logging extension call by invoking the method through an interface or public API that returns the instance as an interface or base type. However, the base class DatabaseManagerBase is also internal abstract, so that won't help.

Given these constraints, I will write a test that mocks ILogger and calls the TaskCheckpointBasedOnAofSizeLimitAsync method via reflection to invoke the internal method and verify the logger call. This is a workaround to test the internal class without changing its accessibility.

I will submit a test file that uses reflection to invoke the internal method and verify the logger call. This will cover the LogInformation call on line 226 as requested.

